<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5804" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">būcĭnum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bucc-</span></b> ), i, n.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The sound</i> or <i>blast of a
			trumpet</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 33, 52, § 103</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 10, 10, §
			20</span></i>.—Hence, ad Bucinum, <i>a quarter in
				Rome</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 14, 4, 5, § 16</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A shell-fish used in dyeing purple</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9,
				36, 61, § 129 sq.</span></i></div>
